      <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--text-secondary);">Starlink's 10,083 satellites (67.8% of the catalog) create an unprecedented concentration of orbital assets under one operator. This has systemic implications: a single deorbit policy change, operational anomaly, or business disruption could affect two-thirds of all active spacecraft. Policy advisors should consider whether current licensing frameworks adequately address concentration-of-risk scenarios at this scale.</p>
